        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: G. D. Spradlin, Marlon Brando, Soo Yong, Al Pacino, Charlton Heston, George C. Scott, Johnny Depp\n- Films: The Good Earth, A Streetcar Named Desire, On the Waterfront, Love Is a Many-Splendored Thing, Sayonara, The Godfather, Viva Zapata!\n- Topics: acting credits, co-stars, award-winning performances\n\nFacts:\n- Soo Yong appeared in the film The Good Earth in 1937.\n- Marlon Brando performed in A Streetcar Named Desire in 1951.\n- Marlon Brando won an Academy Award for playing Terry Malloy in On the Waterfront in 1954.\n- Soo Yong appeared in Love Is a Many-Splendored Thing in 1955.\n- Sayonara is a 1957 Technicolor American film in Technirama starring Marlon Brando.\n- Soo Yong appeared in Sayonara in 1957.\n- Marlon Brando won an Academy Award for playing Vito Corleone in The Godfather in 1972.\n- G. D. Spradlin is credited in more than 70 television and film productions.\n- G. D. Spradlin performed alongside actors including Marlon Brando, Al Pacino, Charlton Heston, George C. Scott, and Johnny Depp.",
